{
 "description": "Live call subtitles (protocols/mgcommands.h, Live call subtitles; Live call only). Hex strings are whole Control payloads, command byte first. messages: each encodes to hex and parses to fields; malformed: each must be rejected. splits: the reply text from from_offset, split into words (each with the whitespace after it, byte offsets, a word longer than max(4, min(255, max_words_bytes - 11)) bytes cut at code point boundaries), each word given the listed show_at, then packed into the listed words messages (max_words_bytes counts from the reply id; at most 255 words; REPLACE on the first message only, FINAL on the last only). reveal: a device model; after each step the revealed text must equal text. Frame numbers are mg_video_frame_header's 16 bits, extended to 32 by counting wraps over every received frame since the stream started: frame_received is a frame header received (decoded or dropped), the only step that extends the count, and frame_shown shows a frame received earlier with the number its receipt gave it (showing is not another receipt). A word is revealed once a shown frame reaches show_at (serial comparison), or the reply's clock does in the ms domain. Subtitle mode begins with state 1 (each reveal case lists it first): words, reply_end and clock received outside subtitle mode are ignored (counted), and state 0 drops everything and ends the mode. lock and unlock are the user's own passcode lock (locked: true on every step while it is up): nothing shows over it and no subtitle message wakes or unlocks it; the words wait for the unlock, and a reply whose reply_end moment comes while locked is dropped. Generated by mg_subtitle_ref.py.",
